# Claim: an `Enum.Variant` path takes its enum from the owner that declares it. DurationUnit comes from the compiler-owned unit enum, HookDecision from the compiler-owned decision hook cases, and NetError and NetDNSError from the core.net source declarations, which the program loads with `use net: core.net` and names bare. Each path builds the right case on o0, o1 and o2.
# Hand-derived: 1500ms is 1500 milliseconds and 1 whole second. The decision built for true is Transform(2) and the one for false is Cancel. The two DNS errors print their net error messages.
fixture: EnumPathsResolveThroughTheirOwners.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = enum_paths_resolve_through_their_owners.out # o0
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = enum_paths_resolve_through_their_owners.out # o1
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = enum_paths_resolve_through_their_owners.out # o2
